{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of your OB-GYN team members. I know you just came in from triage. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Honestly, pretty low. I’ve been struggling since my dad passed. I was doing better with ECT before, but now the anxiety and sadness are back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry about your loss. It makes sense that this would be incredibly hard. We’ve reviewed your history — you’ve been through a lot. We’re here to support you and your baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just want to feel stable again. I was on perphenazine, but it made me restless. The ECT last time helped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the psychiatry team is planning to restart ECT. It’s considered safe in pregnancy with fetal monitoring. We’ll do it on Labor and Delivery so we can watch the baby closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds okay. But what if something goes wrong with the baby during the treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor the fetal heart rate the whole time. If it shows any signs of distress, we’ll stop and reassess. But the risk of untreated depression is higher for both you and the baby than the ECT itself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I just want to do what’s safest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We do too. Also, your lab results show your thyroid is underactive — TSH is high at 9.5. We’d like to start you on levothyroxine. It’s important for your mood and the baby’s brain development."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know I had thyroid issues. Is that why I’ve been so tired?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be part of it. Hypothyroidism can cause fatigue, depression, and brain fog. We’ll start the medication today and check your levels again in a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll take it. Anything else I should know?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium is a bit low, but we’re watching it. And your white count is slightly elevated, but no signs of infection. We’ll keep an eye on everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-03-03 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How did you sleep after yesterday’s admission?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-03-03 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I guess. A little anxious about the ECT today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-03-03 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally normal. You’ll be under anesthesia, so you won’t feel anything. We’ll monitor you and the baby closely. The team is experienced with this in pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-03-03 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And this is unilateral — is that safer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-03-03 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, unilateral targets one side of the brain and tends to have fewer memory side effects. We’ll start there and adjust if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-03-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the ECT today. The seizure was adequate, and the baby’s heart rate stayed stable the whole time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-03-03 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-03-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring everything closely. The psychiatry team noted you seemed more present afterward. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-03-07 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back for your second ECT. How have you been feeling this week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-03-07 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better, honestly. Less heavy. I cried yesterday, but it felt… healthier, like I could process things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-03-07 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. Emotions coming through more clearly can be a sign of improvement. Keep going — we’re seeing a good response."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-03-10 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Third treatment today. Your blood pressure has been creeping up — it was 142/90 this morning. We’re watching for preeclampsia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-03-10 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I’ve been so focused on my mood I didn’t even notice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-03-10 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re being cautious. High BP in pregnancy can affect the placenta. We’ll check your urine for protein and monitor your symptoms — headaches, vision changes, swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-03-10 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No headaches or vision stuff. A little swelling in my ankles, but that’s been there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-03-10 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’ll keep monitoring. The ECT is helping your mood, but if your BP stays high, we might need to deliver sooner than planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-03-13 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine showed protein, and uric acid is elevated. We’re now diagnosing mild preeclampsia. Given your gestational age, we may need to induce soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-03-13 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Is the baby okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-03-13 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, baby’s heart rate is strong. But preeclampsia can worsen quickly, so we’d rather deliver safely than wait. You’re at 36 weeks — that’s far enough along."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-03-13 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess I’m ready, in a way. I just want this over with."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-03-15 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had another ECT yesterday, and the psychiatry team said your mood is much improved. That’s great news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-03-15 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel… clearer. Like I can think again. I even laughed at a silly thought last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-03-15 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. But your blood pressure is still high, and labs confirm preeclampsia. We’re going to start induction tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-03-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting with Cytotec to soften the cervix. This might take a while — you could be in labor for hours or even a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-03-16 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Is the ECT stopping now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-03-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll pause it during labor and recovery. The psychiatry team will follow up after delivery to see if you need more sessions as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-03-17 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re making progress — you’re 4 cm dilated. We’re starting Pitocin to help things along."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-03-17 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s exhausting. But I’m glad it’s happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-03-18 03:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re fully dilated. Time to push."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-03-18 03:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Congratulations — it’s a healthy baby girl. She’s crying strong and breathing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-03-18 03:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… hi, sweetie. I can’t believe she’s here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. We had to manually remove the placenta — it was retained. But no hemorrhage, so that’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not common, but it happens. We’re giving you oxytocin to help your uterus contract. You’ll need to keep an eye on bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-03-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is coming down, which is great. But we’re seeing some signs of chorioamnionitis — low-grade fever and elevated white count."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-03-19 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-03-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a mild one in the membranes. We’re starting antibiotics just in case. The urine culture was clean, so that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-03-20 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry stopped by. They’d like to do one more ECT session while you’re still here, since you responded so well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-03-20 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Now? I just had a baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-03-20 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s optional, but they think it could help stabilize you postpartum, when mood risks are high. It’s safe — we’ll monitor you and the baby during breastfeeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-03-20 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, if it helps. I don’t want to crash after all this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-03-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ECT went well. You’re doing incredibly — managing recovery, a newborn, and treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-03-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your fever is gone, and white count is improving. We’ll finish the antibiotics. Also, your thyroid levels are stabilizing on levothyroxine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-03-21 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I feel stronger every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-03-22 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you a thyroid hormone infusion to keep your levels steady. You’ll continue the pill at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-03-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve got a small vaginal tear that needed repair. It’s minor, but we did a quick procedure to close it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-03-23 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. I didn’t even feel it. Is it healing okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-03-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s clean and healing well. Just keep up with perineal care and pain meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-03-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing so well. We’re planning to discharge tomorrow. You’ll go home on quetiapine instead of perphenazine — it’s better for postpartum mood stability."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-03-24 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-03-24 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Outpatient follow-up. You’ll continue as needed. And your psychiatrist will monitor your bipolar symptoms closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-03-24 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared but also hopeful. I want to be a good mom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2172-03-24 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re already showing so much strength. You’ve been through an immense challenge and come out the other side. We’ll make sure you have support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2172-03-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your labs are stable. BP is normal. You’re cleared to go home. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2172-03-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just — thank you. For not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2172-03-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re so proud of you. Keep in touch with your team. You’ve got this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2172-03-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nursing is finalizing your discharge meds: quetiapine, levothyroxine, prenatal vitamins, and pain relief as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2172-03-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll take them every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2172-03-25 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Just remember — postpartum is a marathon, not a sprint. Call if you feel low or anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2172-03-25 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I want to stay well for my daughter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2172-03-25 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re strong, and you’re not alone. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2172-03-25 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. Really."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself and your baby. You’ve earned this moment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge order is in. Social work will help you with transportation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My mom’s picking me up. I’m nervous but excited."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely normal. You’ve got a great support system. Keep leaning on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check — you’re alert, walking fine, and your mood is stable. You’re cleared for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again. I feel like I can breathe now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2172-03-25 13:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve worked so hard for this. Go home and rest. You’ve got this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2172-03-25 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll be checking in with your outpatient team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2172-03-25 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep my appointments. I want to stay healthy."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-03-02 12:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-03-25 14:12:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 36-week pregnant patient with a history of bipolar disorder and recent bereavement was admitted for recurrent severe depression and akathisia, with plans to resume electroconvulsive therapy (ECT). She was found to have hypothyroidism, which was treated with levothyroxine. She received multiple ECT sessions with good psychiatric response. During her stay, she developed gestational hypertension and preeclampsia, prompting induction of labor at 36 weeks. She delivered vaginally, required manual extraction of a retained placenta, and had a minor vaginal laceration repaired. Postpartum, she developed mild chorioamnionitis, treated with antibiotics. Her mood stabilized on quetiapine, and she was discharged home in stable condition with outpatient psychiatric follow-up and a plan for continued ECT as needed.",
    "problems": [
      "Other mental disorders complicating childbirth",
      "Single live birth",
      "Chorioamnionitis, third trimester, not applicable or unspecified",
      "Gestational [pregnancy-induced] hypertension without significant proteinuria, third trimester",
      "Unspecified pre-eclampsia, third trimester",
      "Obstetric high vaginal laceration alone",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "36 weeks gestation of pregnancy",
      "Endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases complicating pregnancy, third trimester",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Retained placenta without hemorrhage"
    ]
  }
}
